From: arena-ai-coding-agent <arena-ai-coding-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 07:29:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Restrict OpenCode Zen bridge to the model adapter only

Drop the anonymous Exa MCP web-search plugin from the OPENCODE_ZEN=1
integration so the bridge installs and activates only
@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm-opencode. Also keep the adapter normalizations: named
exports only (remove export default apply) and SSE tool-call name overwrite
instead of accumulation, which otherwise produces web_searchweb_search and
breaks model tool calls.
---
 README.md                     |  4 +++-
 docs/index.html               |  2 +-
 install.sh                    | 16 +++++--------
 tools/enable-opencode-zen.mjs | 45 ++++++++++++++++++++---------------
 4 files changed, 36 insertions(+), 31 deletions(-)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 567345e..1fca0d9 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@ BUILD=0 ./install.sh "$HOME/dsh-remote-web"
 
 ### Opt-in OpenCode Zen bridge
 
-Pass `OPENCODE_ZEN=1` to also add the [DSH OpenCode Zen bridge](https://github.com/DHS-M/dsh-opencode-zen) from the same organization. It installs the standalone `@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm-opencode` adapter, the anonymous Exa MCP web-search plugin, and points the default agent model at `opencode-zen` / `big-pickle` through a local loopback route.
+Pass `OPENCODE_ZEN=1` to also add the [DSH OpenCode Zen bridge](https://github.com/DHS-M/dsh-opencode-zen) from the same organization. It installs only the standalone `@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm-opencode` model adapter and points the default agent model at `opencode-zen` / `big-pickle` through a local loopback route. Web-search plugins are intentionally excluded.
 
 ```bash
 OPENCODE_ZEN=1 BUILD=1 ./install.sh "$HOME/dsh-remote-web"
@@ -37,6 +37,8 @@ node <dsh-opencode-zen>/zen_shim.js
 
 If you are not calling the real OpenCode Zen endpoint, the bridge still works against an OpenAI-compatible `/v1` server bound to `http://127.0.0.1:8791`.
 
+The enable step also normalizes the upstream standalone adapter's SSE tool-call name handling (`state.name += …` → `state.name = …`). Without that fix a normal one-chunk `web_search` tool call is recorded as `web_searchweb_search` and rejected as an unknown tool. The adapter still removes the DSH-incompatible `export default apply` so the Cordis loader reads its named `inject`/`name` metadata.
+
 ## Run the web interface
 
 ```bash
